      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is also well above the usual maximum single dose of about 850 mg to 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nCould the intended dose have been one of these?\n- **850 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **500 mg** by mouth three times daily with meals\n- **1000 mg** by mouth twice daily with meals\n- **1700 mg total per day**, divided (for example, 850 mg twice daily)\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you verified the dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
